  "ingredients": [
    "4 lemons, halved",
    "2 medium sweet onions (such as Vidalia®), quartered",
    "4 serrano chiles, split in 1/2 lengthwise and seeds and membranes removed",
    "2 heads garlic, peeled and halved",
    "2 bunches fresh thyme, tied with string",
    "1.6666667461395 cups seafood seasoning (such as Old Bay®), or more to taste",
    "6 teaspoons kosher salt, or more to taste",
    "6 bay leaves",
    "3 pounds medium red potatoes, cut in 1/2",
    "5 (13 ounce) packages smoked kielbasa sausage, cut into 2-inch pieces",
    "6 ears sweet corn, halved",
    "30 littleneck clams, scrubbed",
    "4 pounds jumbo shrimp, deveined, tail on",
    "2.5 pounds Alaskan king crab legs"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Fill a very large stockpot fitted with a basket insert with about 8 quarts of water, or about halfway full. Squeeze lemons into the water, tossing the halves in too. Add onions, chiles, garlic, thyme, seafood seasoning, kosher salt, and bay leaves; bring to a boil over medium-high heat. Reduce heat and simmer for 10 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/p50ZIat6nxOaAAhQlkx_6_0zk14=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/279460-Old-Bay-Seafood-Boil-ddmfs-131-step1-25add6ad4ec742c98ed529ed5e4c92eb.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/279460/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir potatoes into the pot and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/jFM2w3R0z_WmS3BAdqdUfTvspng=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/279460-Old-Bay-Seafood-Boil-ddmfs-133-step2-option-27b04e1ba84f4557a62f8f912cfcb7b0.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/279460/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Next, add sausage and corn; cook another 5 minutes, making sure everything stays covered with the liquid.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/5eu-SRVghHU2n6SXcCA0jNlYP_s=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/279460-Old-Bay-Seafood-Boil-ddmfs-134-step3-7cd081c656b149bf9536d2822ab6dc50.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/279460/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add clams and boil until they open, about 8 minutes. Toss in shrimp and shut off the heat. Cover the pot and let shrimp steep in the flavor for 10 minutes, adding crab in the last 5 minutes (press them into the liquid).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Ss7FxFlN4NRffhnDMdHybCAujM0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/279460-Old-Bay-Seafood-Boil-ddmfs-136-step5-02763dd4882046ff8a9fddb7a8b7c7c6.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/279460/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Drain and spread crab, shrimp, sausage, clams, corn, potatoes, and onions out on a newspaper-covered table or on three large serving trays. Sprinkle with a dusting of Old Bay or provide for individual use.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/XDFvpo7BXQ7_s920fAp28qox0PY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/279460-Old-Bay-Seafood-Boil-ddmfs-139-4x3-aa189a5c09104659957fe6fcb715c4bd.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/279460/step_05.webp"
    }
